cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "OptoNet: Deep Learning Predicts and Designs Neuron-Type-Specific Responses to Optogenetic Stimulation"
message: "If you use this benchmark, code or manuscript, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Ali
    given-names: Basit
    email: basitali.262713@gmail.com
    affiliation: "Abdul Wali Khan University, Mardan, Pakistan"
repository-code: "https://github.com/basitali08/optonet"
url: "https://github.com/basitali08/optonet"
abstract: >-
  OptoNet is a reproducible benchmark and model suite for predicting and
  designing neuronal responses to optogenetic stimulation. It combines a
  biophysically grounded simulator (AdEx neuron with a two-state ChR2
  photocurrent), 61,000 stimulation trials across nine protocol families and
  three cell types, classical and deep sequence models (GLM, dilated CNN,
  Conv-LSTM, OptoFormer), out-of-distribution generalisation tests, uncertainty
  quantification, few-shot cross-cell-type transfer and model-in-the-loop
  stimulation design.
keywords:
  - optogenetics
  - channelrhodopsin
  - computational neuroscience
  - deep learning
  - neural encoding
  - spiking neural networks
license: MIT
